  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "lines": [
        [
          {
            "refs": [
              "w1"
            ],
            "text": "The One who leads the spirit hosts,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w2"
            ],
            "text": "the giver of wide fame,"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "refs": [
              "w3"
            ],
            "text": "who cleanses the merit and the sin of the people who live in Kāśī,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w4"
            ],
            "text": "the all-pervading Lord,"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "refs": [
              "w5"
            ],
            "text": "skilled in the path of right conduct,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w6"
            ],
            "text": "the ancient one,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w7"
            ],
            "text": "the lord of the world:"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "refs": [
              "w10"
            ],
            "text": "I worship"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w9"
            ],
            "text": "Kālabhairava,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w8"
            ],
            "text": "the supreme lord of the city of Kāśī."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "bhavartha": "Kālabhairava leads the hosts of spirits and gives wide fame. He cleanses both the merit and the sin of the people who live in Kāśī, and He is the Lord who is everywhere. He knows the path of right conduct well, He is ancient, and He is the lord of the world. The singer worships Him: Kālabhairava, the supreme lord of the city of Kāśī."
    },
    "hi": {
      "lines": [
        [
          {
            "refs": [
              "w1"
            ],
            "text": "जो भूत-गणों के नायक हैं,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w2"
            ],
            "text": "विशाल कीर्ति देने वाले हैं,"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "refs": [
              "w3"
            ],
            "text": "जो काशी में बसने वाले लोगों के पुण्य और पाप का शोधन करते हैं,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w4"
            ],
            "text": "जो सर्वव्यापी प्रभु हैं,"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "refs": [
              "w5"
            ],
            "text": "जो नीति-मार्ग के ज्ञाता हैं,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w6"
            ],
            "text": "पुरातन हैं,"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w7"
            ],
            "text": "जगत् के स्वामी हैं,"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "refs": [
              "w8"
            ],
            "text": "काशी नगरी के अधिपति"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w9"
            ],
            "text": "कालभैरव को"
          },
          {
            "refs": [
              "w10"
            ],
            "text": "मैं भजता हूँ।"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "bhavartha": "कालभैरव भूत-गणों के नायक हैं और विशाल कीर्ति देने वाले हैं। काशी में बसने वाले लोगों के पुण्य और पाप, दोनों का वे शोधन करते हैं, और वे सर्वव्यापी प्रभु हैं। वे नीति के मार्ग को भली-भाँति जानते हैं, पुरातन हैं और जगत् के स्वामी हैं। ऐसे काशी नगरी के अधिपति कालभैरव को भक्त भजता है।"
    }
  },
  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "refs": [
        "w1"
      ],
      "kind": "wordplay",
      "body": {
        "en": "*Bhūta* means 'what has come to be', so it names two very different crowds. It is any living being, and a *bhūta-saṅgha* can be the whole mass of all that lives. It is also a spirit: a ghost of the dead, a goblin. So the line can be heard both ways. He leads the hosts of ghosts and spirits, and He leads every creature there is.",
        "hi": "*भूत* का अर्थ है 'जो हो चुका, जो बना है', इसलिए यह दो बहुत अलग समूहों का नाम है। यह कोई भी प्राणी है, और *भूत-सङ्घ* सारे जीवों का पूरा समूह हो सकता है। यह प्रेत भी है: मरे हुए की छाया, पिशाच। इसलिए पंक्ति दोनों तरह सुनी जा सकती है। वे भूत-प्रेतों के गणों के भी नायक हैं, और हर प्राणी के भी।"
      },
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "mw-bhuta",
          "locator": "MW bhūta, p. 761,3",
          "quote": "a spirit (good or evil), the ghost of a deceased person, a demon, imp, goblin"
        },
        {
          "source": "mw-bhuta",
          "locator": "MW bhūta, p. 761,3",
          "quote": "that which is or exists, any living being"
        },
        {
          "source": "mw-bhutasamgha",
          "locator": "MW bhūta-saṃgha, p. 762,2",
          "quote": "the totality of beings or of the elements"
        },
        {
          "source": "shlokam-kalabhairava",
          "locator": "verse 8, word meanings",
          "quote": "भूत (bhūta) – ghosts"
        },
        {
          "source": "gitapress-shiv-stotra-ratnakar",
          "locator": "p. 204, verse 8, Hindi translation",
          "quote": "जो समस्त प्राणिसमुदायके नायक हैं"
        }
      ],
      "confidence": "medium"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "refs": [
        "w3"
      ],
      "kind": "theology",
      "body": {
        "en": "Picture a refiner bent over his fire, or a clerk settling an account. *Śodhaka* is 'one who cleanses', and its family of words covers refining metal, sifting and checking, paying off a debt, wiping out. What He clears here is the record of everyone who lives in Kāśī: their merit (*puṇya*) and their sin (*pāpa*).\n\nBoth, not sin alone. Read deeper, once both are cleared the Self is left pure, tied by no deed at all ([the cord of karma](#v5-a2)).",
        "hi": "कल्पना कीजिए: भट्ठी पर झुका धातु निखारने वाला, या हिसाब चुकता करता मुनीम। *शोधक* यानी 'शुद्ध करने वाला', और इसी शब्द-परिवार के अर्थ हैं धातु को निखारना, छानना-परखना, कर्ज़ चुकाना, मिटा देना। यहाँ वे काशी में बसने वाले हर व्यक्ति का लेखा साफ़ करते हैं: उसका पुण्य और उसका पाप।\n\nदोनों, केवल पाप नहीं। गहरे अर्थ में, दोनों के मिटने पर आत्मा शुद्ध रह जाती है, किसी कर्म से बँधी नहीं ([कर्म की डोर](#v5-a2))।"
      },
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "mw-shodhaka",
          "locator": "MW śodhaka, p. 1091,3",
          "quote": "a purifier"
        },
        {
          "source": "mw-shodhana",
          "locator": "MW śodhana, p. 1091,3",
          "quote": "refining (as of metals for chemical or medicinal purposes)"
        },
        {
          "source": "mw-shodhana",
